<p>President Trump and Russian President Vladimir Putin held a phone call on April 29 that lasted more than 90 minutes and covered Russia&#x27;s war in Ukraine and the conflict involving Iran, Kremlin aide Yuri Ushakov and Trump said. The Kremlin said Putin either proposed or was ready to declare a temporary ceasefire in Ukraine around Russia&#x27;s May 9 Victory Day commemorations; Trump said he had discussed what he called a small ceasefire, while Meduza reported that Moscow and Trump differed over who originated the idea. No agreement from Ukraine was announced, and The New York Times reported that it was unclear whether Ukraine would accept Moscow&#x27;s terms after earlier truces broke down amid competing accusations of violations. Business Recorder and The Express Tribune, citing Reuters, said Putin announced a similar three-day truce last year that was not agreed with Kyiv. On Iran, Ushakov said Putin put forward ideas on Iran&#x27;s nuclear program, backed Trump&#x27;s decision to extend a ceasefire with Iran, and warned that renewed U.S. or Israeli military action would have extremely harmful consequences. Trump told reporters the call focused more on Ukraine than Iran and said Putin wanted to help on Iran, but that he told the Russian leader to end the Ukraine war first.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gLrvvl1ICHORslBjrtGZTXfnnJ_YHj8lyA8qGlTaW35hL_5teh0YLr6DE8nEg91vkDWYzFBnSbWLvMda7Xc8UnFY5pUrh2B9oEAgbzwSUFfZ_si9cQatN20wfgyQYRJuLUv89TPIH-ETsMCNgU_mhlEZ0cIPorurcs0RlxpNvKcpgtxxwsHEIojUK4SsZrZDQ3F2SPhzhl1TKAmItFdHxdN8w3Hdd1MsxPRO15ptNdgqZNLcUUmU-IhkmoRgzKsFUWJkA1rhtihXzEsFSQ' alt='Recruits practice military skills at a training ground near the frontline in the Zaporizhzhia region, Ukraine, on Wednesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Parade detail: Tocka reported that this year&#x27;s Moscow Victory Day parade was expected to take place without tanks or other heavy military equipment for the first time since 1945, citing Russia&#x27;s Defense Ministry&#x27;s reference to the &quot;current operational situation&quot;.</li><li>Front-line claim: Kremlin accounts said Putin told Trump that Russian forces held the strategic initiative along the front line and were pushing back Ukrainian positions.</li><li>Deal claim: Accounts citing the Kremlin readout said Trump told reporters he believed a deal to end Russia&#x27;s war against Ukraine was close.</li><li>Kyiv contact: Tocka reported that no call between Trump and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky was scheduled at the time, though a Kyiv Independent source said that could change quickly.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kremlin: Yuri Ushakov said Putin condemned the reported attempt on President Trump&#x27;s life and described political violence as unacceptable. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639267-putin-trump-phone-talks/'>RT</a>)</li><li>President Trump: After the call, Trump said the U.S. was &quot;going to come up with a solution relatively quickly&quot; over its conflict with Iran. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/diplomacy/article/3351913/trump-says-he-had-good-talk-putin-iran-and-ukraine'>SCMP</a>)</li><li>Kyiv-linked reporting: Tocka reported that Putin had rejected a full and unconditional ceasefire proposed by Kyiv while continuing to offer temporary, limited pauses. (<a href='https://tocka.com.mk/vesti/554622/putin-i-tramp-razgovarale-cas-i-polovina-moskva-predlozila-primirje-za-denot-na-pobedata'>Tocka</a>)</li><li>BBC Russian: BBC Russian said Trump&#x27;s post-call remarks appeared to mix up Ukraine and Iran. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/russian/articles/cx21kw3n6y2o'>BBC Russian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639267-putin-trump-phone-talks/'>Putin and Trump speak by phone – Kremlin aide</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/29/world/europe/ukraine-russia-ceasefire-trump-putin.html'>Trump and Putin Call for a Brief Cease-Fire in Ukraine</a> - nytimes.com</li><li>